### Initialize CanvasRenderer on UI Thread

Source: https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/wear_hl=bn

Introduces `CanvasRenderer.uiThreadInit` which is called once on the UI thread before any rendering occurs. This method facilitates easier initialization of the renderer and sharing state between the `Renderer` and `CanvasComplication`. It simplifies setup for rendering components.

```java
public class CanvasRenderer {

    /**
     * Called once on the UI thread before any calls to render.
     * Use this method for any UI thread initialization.
     */
    public void uiThreadInit() {
        // Perform UI thread initialization here
        // For example: setup UI resources, initialize listeners, etc.
        Log.d("CanvasRenderer", "UI thread initialization complete.");
    }

    // The render method would be called after uiThreadInit
    public void render(Canvas canvas, Rect bounds, long time) {
        // Rendering logic
    }
}

public class CanvasComplication {
    private Renderer renderer;

    public void setRenderer(Renderer renderer) {
        this.renderer = renderer;
        if (renderer instanceof CanvasRenderer) {
            ((CanvasRenderer) renderer).uiThreadInit(); // Call init if it's a CanvasRenderer
        }
        onRendererCreated(); // Call onRendererCreated
    }

    /**
     * Called when the renderer is set, making it easier to share state.
     */
    protected void onRendererCreated() {
        // Initialize or share state with the renderer here
    }
}

```

