### OpenGL-based Framebuffer Rendering with GLFrameBufferRenderer (Android)

Source: https://developer.android.com/jetpack/androidx/releases/graphics_hl=fr

Introduces `GLFrameBufferRenderer` for OpenGL-based rendering, managing swapchain configurations, pixel formats, and `SurfaceControl`. This API is suitable for scenarios requiring direct OpenGL rendering to a buffer that can be presented.

```java
GLFrameBufferRenderer renderer = new GLFrameBufferRenderer(
    width, height, surfaceControl, eglContext, pixelFormat);

renderer.renderFrame(frameBuffer -> {
    // OpenGL rendering commands
});

renderer.release();
```

